  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase-out PADANE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PADANE&apos;s exit strategy  (3 mln euros) has been designed to maximise the consolidation of what has been achieved based on two main objectives:
1.	Objective 1: To perpetuate the effects that can be consolidated in the regions, which accounts for 80% of the activity budget.
2.	Objective 2: To make the most of strategic achievements as a Dutch legacy, which accounts for 20% of the activity budget.
Ad 1:
1.	Supporting the most promising local networks to increasing their autonomy and capacity to deliver sustainable services to relevant actors.
2.	Assisting the most promising beneficiaries of the Innovation Fund  in implementing their business plans and establishing links with financial institutions 
3.	Facilitate the adoption of the most successful innovations 
Ad 2:
4.	Encourage the integration of PADANE approaches, tools, knowledge and functions 
5.	If legal approval is granted by ENABEL, PADANE will contribute to the preparation of the PAVE program</narrative>
  </description>
